@blogdesign7126 But yeah, its got lower population because most immigrants prefer a warmer climate but also because there wasn't any sugar plantations in Canada. Most of the population of the US, Mexico, Central America and South America did not immigrate there by choice. They were slaves who were forcefully relocated there to cultivate sugar. 
Canada was pretty much the only country where slaves weren't forcefully brought over.  Everyone of the Canadians were people who came by choice. And its a lot harder to populate land when you can only take volunteers. Especially land with such cold winter. 
That's the real reason that Canada's population is and has always been so much lower then that of the US. Remove the slave descendants, yes all of them and you suddenly get populations they are about the same as Canada's. The US would still have more because it has the best lands. But Mexico? It might even be lower then Canada if you remove every slave descendants. Brazil is even worse. Without the slave descendants, its population would fall to around 10 million or maybe even less.
